      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "🌍 Vietnamese envoy calls for student exchange program between Imam Khomeini, Hanoi universities\n\n📌 Qazvin, IRNA — Vietnamese Ambassador to Iran Nguyen Luong Ngoc has proposed establishing academic cooperation between Imam Khomeini International University and Hanoi University to expand educational and cultural exchanges between the two countries.\n\nSpeaking during a visit to Imam Khomeini International University in Qazvin on Sunday, the ambassador praised the university’s academic and educational capacities and expressed hope that more Vietnamese students would have the opportunity to study there.\n​\nHe said the university offered excellent academic programs and that Vietnamese students could benefit from its educational opportunities.\n​\nNgoc also welcomed the presence of international students at the Iranian university, describing it as a source of pride.\n​\nThe ambassador further highlighted Vietnam’s capacity for university-level education and Persian-language studies, noting that Hanoi University has a School of Oriental Studies where Persian is taught.\n​\nHe added that Hanoi University had already signed a memorandum of understanding with the University of Tehran, expressing hope that academic ties could also be established with Imam Khomeini International University.\n\n📲 @Irna_en​",
